S(6,"w6t2","short",2,"Why did opera develop as a new genre in Soviet Kazakhstan?",[["new genre","new"],["soviet","national in form","state"],["folk","epic","melod"],["european","western","classical"],["theatre","decade","moscow"]],"Opera was a new genre for Kazakh culture, whose traditional music was küy and song. Soviet policy promoted 'national in form, socialist in content' culture, including national operas; composers combined Kazakh folk melodies and epics (Kyz Zhibek, Birzhan–Sara, Abai) with the European opera form; the Kazakh Musical Theatre and the 1936 Decade of Kazakh Art in Moscow made Kazakh opera famous.");
