S(7,"w7t3","short",2,"Name and define the four dimensions of cultural intelligence.",[["metacognitive"],["cognitive","knowledge"],["motivational","interest","confidence"],["behavioral","behaviour","flex"]],"Metacognitive CQ – the mental capability to acquire and understand cultural knowledge; Cognitive CQ – knowledge about cultures, their similarities and differences; Motivational CQ – interest and confidence in functioning effectively in intercultural contexts; Behavioral CQ – the capability to flex verbal and non-verbal behaviors in intercultural interactions (Earley & Ang 2003).");
S(7,"w7t3","compare",2,"Explain the difference between IQ, EQ and CQ.",[["iq","cognitive","test","age"],["eq","emotion"],["cq","intercultural","cultures"]],"IQ is a score from standardized tests measuring cognitive abilities relative to one's age group; EQ is the ability to manage one's own emotions and understand others' emotions; CQ is the capability to function effectively in intercultural contexts. A person can have high IQ and EQ at home but still misread cultural signals abroad – CQ is specific to cultural diversity.");
