M(8,"w8t2","theory",2,"Khan Shatyr connects to Kazakh identity because it…",["reinterprets a nomadic tent with modern materials","is a copy of a European cathedral","is a Soviet monument","symbolizes the golden egg"],"Ancestral heritage + cutting-edge technology.");
TF(8,"w8t2","people",3,"According to the lecture, Baiterek was designed by Norman Foster.",false,"False – the lecture names Akmyrza Rustembekov. Foster designed Khan Shatyr and the Palace of Peace.");
S(8,"w8t2","apply",3,"Explain, with at least two examples, how Astana's architecture reflects Kazakhstan's cultural identity.",[["baiterek","tree","egg"],["khan shatyr","tent","nomad"],["palace","pyramid","peace","religion","toleran"],["mangilik","arch","eternal"],["identity","code","symbol"]],"Astana's buildings translate cultural codes into modern forms. Baiterek (golden egg on the Tree of Life) uses Turkic myth to symbolize rebirth and the new capital; Khan Shatyr reinterprets the nomadic khan's tent in modern materials; the Palace of Peace and Reconciliation expresses interfaith harmony and multi-ethnic tolerance; the Mängilik El arch (2011) expresses the 'Eternal Country' idea. Together they show identity balancing tradition and globalization.");
M(8,"w8t3","def",1,"In the Week 8 lecture, a cultural code is…",["a set of symbols and images that pass information within a group","a law on culture","a list of values","a Hofstede dimension"],"Cultural code.");
M(8,"w8t3","apply",2,"'Taza Kazakhstan' is an example of which value direction?",["ecology culture","digital transformation","multiculturalism","hustle culture"],"Clean Kazakhstan.");
S(8,"w8t3","apply",2,"Give two practical examples of how Kazakh cultural codes are represented digitally, and one challenge of such representation.",[["e-museum","3d","museum"],["tiktok","instagram","social media","youtube","meme"],["corpus","language","kazakh"],["stereotyp","exotic","commerc","simulacr","misrepresent"]],"Examples: 3D yurts and dombras on e-Museum; Kazakh memes and ornaments in social media; Kazakh National Corpus; World Nomad Games broadcasts. Challenges: stereotyping/exoticization, commercialization, simulacra replacing real culture, dominance of Russian/English content.");
M(8,"w8t4","people",1,"Geert Hofstede developed his model by studying employees of…",["IBM in more than 50 countries","Google in 20 countries","the UN in 100 countries","Nixdorf in Germany"],"IBM.");
M(8,"w8t4","people",2,"The sixth dimension, Indulgence vs Restraint, was developed together with…",["Michael Minkov","Michael H. Bond","Soon Ang","Kalervo Oberg"],"Minkov.");
