S(8,"w8t5","short",3,"Can Kazakhstan's growing IT and digital creative industries preserve national culture while competing in the global market? Give arguments for both sides and a conclusion.",[["glocal","adapt","local"],["homogeniz","uniform","global format","english"],["game","cinema","film","music","ai"],["identity","preserv","heritage"],["econom","market","compet"],["conclu","balance","therefore","yes"]],"FOR: technology lowers barriers to reach global audiences; glocal products with authentic nomadic/Silk Road stories sell; IT growth funds culture (Astana Hub, games, cinema like 'Tomiris', music like Dimash, Kazakh AI models); digital preservation provides raw material. AGAINST: pressure to adopt global formats and English (homogenization), commercialization and stereotypes, small market and brain drain, dependence on foreign platforms. CONCLUSION: possible through a glocal strategy – global technology + local content, state support for Kazakh-language content and heritage data, education linking IT and humanities.");

