S(9,"w9t2","compare",3,"Compare hustle culture, meme culture and cancel culture: give a definition, one positive and one negative effect for each.",[["hustle","productiv"],["meme","imitation","dawkins"],["cancel","withdraw","boycott"],["burnout","stress"],["humor","critique","creativ","community"],["mob","forgive","disproportion","bully"]],"Hustle culture glorifies constant productivity (+ ambition/entrepreneurship, − burnout). Meme culture spreads units of imitation (Dawkins) as humorous reactions (+ social critique, community, − misinformation/out-of-context humiliation). Cancel culture is collective withdrawal of support after perceived offense (+ accountability, voice for victims, − mob justice, no forgiveness, overlaps with cyberbullying).");
