S(9,"w9t4","short",3,"What was the Digital Kazakhstan state program? Describe its goals, directions and one achievement and one limitation, distinguishing it from earlier and later initiatives.",[["2017","2018","2022"],["standard of living","economy","productivity"],["digital state","e-gov","government"],["silk road","infrastructure"],["human capital","literacy"],["innovat","ecosystem","start"],["divide","security","rural","limitation"],["2006","2023","2029","concept"]],"Approved in Dec 2017 (Decree No. 827) for 2018–2022, it aimed to raise every citizen's standard of living and economic productivity through digital technology. Five directions: digitalization of economic sectors, transition to a digital state, Digital Silk Road (infrastructure), human capital development, innovative ecosystem (17 initiatives, 120 projects). Achievement: most public services online via eGov (top-25 UN e-government ranking). Limitation: digital divide in rural areas and cybersecurity/data-leak risks. It followed the e-government program (eGov.kz 2006) and was succeeded by the Concept of Digital Transformation, ICT and Cybersecurity 2023–2029.");
