S(9,"w9t5","apply",3,"Identify three barriers women face in the IT sector and propose a concrete policy or practice for each, with reference to Kazakhstan.",[["stereotyp"],["pay gap","salary","earn"],["glass ceiling","leadership","senior"],["family","childcare","balance"],["mentor","club","tech girls","techno women","program"],["bias","ai"]],"Barriers: stereotypes from school ('IT is for boys') → girls' coding clubs like Tech Girls and role models (Ada Lovelace, local founders); pay gap → salary transparency and equal-pay audits; glass ceiling → mentoring and women-in-leadership programs (Techno Women, Astana Hub support); work–family balance → flexible/remote work and childcare; biased AI hiring tools → red-teaming and audits (UNESCO playbook).");

