S(10,"w10t1","short",2,"What were the main goals and achievements of the Cultural Heritage (Madeni Mura) program?",[["2004"],["restor","monument"],["archaeolog"],["manuscript","archive","document"],["identity","memory"],["aisha","arystan","babalar","5,000","5000","10,000"]],"Adopted in 2004 on Nazarbayev's initiative (first such program in the CIS), with stages 2004–06, 2007–09, 2009–11. Goals: study, restore and preserve historical-cultural heritage, revive traditions, promote heritage and strengthen national identity. Achievements: restoration of dozens of monuments (Aisha Bibi, Arystan Bab mausoleums), archaeological research, acquisition of about 5,000 manuscripts at first and later 10,000+ archival records from abroad (most from China), publication of the 100-volume 'Babalar Sözi'.");
M(10,"w10t2","date",1,"Kazakhstan's first UNESCO World Heritage site, inscribed in 2003, is…",["the Mausoleum of Khoja Ahmed Yasawi","the Tamgaly petroglyphs","Saryarka","the Silk Roads corridor"],"Yasawi 2003.");
