S(10,"w10t3","short",2,"Why are national sports considered cultural heritage? Use at least three Kazakh examples.",[["nomad","horse","history","origin"],["kokpar","kyz kuu","audaryspak","baiga","kuresi","asyk","togyz"],["identity","values","courage"],["generation","transmi","children","elder"],["nomad games","unesco","preserv"]],"They grew out of nomadic life (horse riding, herding, war training) and carry values like courage, honour and teamwork; they are transmitted between generations at toi and holidays. Examples: kokpar, kyz kuu, audaryspak, kazakh kuresi (UNESCO 2016), asyk atu (2017), togyzkumalak (2020). Today they are preserved through federations, schools, UNESCO lists and the World Nomad Games (Astana 2024).");
M(10,"w10t4","def",2,"The process in which cultures become similar under global influence is called…",["cultural homogenization","cultural ecology","glocalization","syncretism"],"Homogenization ('McDonaldization').");
M(10,"w10t4","compare",3,"Q-pop and ethno-jazz with the dombra are best described as examples of…",["hybridization / glocalization","homogenization","counterculture","cultural relativism"],"Global + local mix.");
S(10,"w10t4","short",3,"Discuss globalization and the future of Kazakh cultural identity using the terms homogenization, glocalization and cultural preservation.",[["homogeniz","uniform"],["glocal","hybrid","robertson"],["preserv","heritage","unesco","madeni"],["identity"],["language","kazakh"],["example","q-pop","nomad games","e-museum","dimash"]],"Globalization can homogenize culture (global brands, English), but also enables glocalization – mixing global forms with Kazakh content (Q-pop, ethno-music, Nomad Games). Cultural preservation (Madeni Mura, UNESCO lists, e-Museum) protects the core. The future of Kazakh identity depends on conscious glocalization: keeping core values and the Kazakh language while expressing them in new global forms.");
S(10,"w10t5","apply",3,"Can tradition and innovation coexist in national culture? Take a position and support it with Kazakh examples and a counterargument.",[["tradition"],["innovat","technolog","modern"],["e-museum","corpus","togyz","khan shatyr","dombra","betashar","3d"],["however","but","risk","although","commerc","authentic"],["coexist","yes","balance"]],"Yes: when innovation serves the meaning of tradition. Examples: e-Museum 3D exhibits, the Kazakh National Corpus, togyzkumalak apps and its UNESCO listing, Khan Shatyr as a modern tent, betashar in modern weddings. Counterargument: commercialization and loss of authenticity, generation gap. Conclusion: coexistence is possible if communities stay the bearers of tradition.");
